# Sonance PowerZone Connect / PowerZone Connect PRO amplifier driver
#
# Controls Sonance's networked DSP amplifiers over the Open API on TCP 7621:
# the PowerZone Connect line (sold as Blaze by Sonance, formerly Blaze Audio)
# and the 70 V / 100 V PowerZone Connect PRO line. Both run the same firmware
# platform: the PRO release notes (2026.18.1) call the first PRO firmware
# "based on the PowerZone Connect 2026.18.1 firmware platform", and Sonance's
# support page files the one Open API document under PowerZone Connect
# amplifiers. The document is Edition 2026.24.1 (June 2026), for API 1.5 and
# firmware 1.8 and later, 2026.x included.
#
# Protocol reference: Sonance "Open API for Installers", Edition 2026.24.1.
# Archived: driver-roadmap/reference-docs/sonance-powerzone-connect-open-api-2026.24.1.{pdf,txt}
#
# Wire format (document chapters 2-4):
#   Plain TCP, one message per line, each ending in "\n". Three reply shapes:
#     +<register> <value>      a value (a GET reply, an INC result, or a push)
#     *<command>               the command succeeded (always last)
#     #<command>|<message>     the command failed; the message usually starts
#                              with an Exxx code (E107: Unknown Parameter)
#   PING answers PONG, then *PING. GET takes a wildcard; the document shows it
#   in the id position (GET IN-*.NAME answers one line per input the amplifier
#   has), which is the only form this driver uses. SET and INC take none.
#   Booleans read 0 / 1 and are written 1 / 0. Strings come back double-quoted
#   and are written quoted; there is no escape, so a value cannot contain a
#   double quote (name parameters refuse one). Floats come back with a
#   per-register number of decimals (-5.00, 1000.000), so every rule reads a
#   plain decimal.
#
# Push, not polling (Principle 2): SUBSCRIBE REG makes the amplifier send
# "+<register> <value>" on this connection whenever any register changes,
# from any client, its web app, a wall controller, GPIO or a preset. A SET is
# echoed to every REG subscriber before its *SET acknowledgement, and an INC
# always answers with the new value, so every write reads itself back with no
# second request. SUBSCRIBE REG is the first start-up line for that reason
# (a SET sent before it gets no echo), and the document does not say a
# subscription replays current values, so the start-up GETs are the initial
# read. The poll re-reads the status registers (the document does not say
# whether they are pushed) and the wall controller levels.
#
# Level meters (the *.DYN.* registers) are subscription-only and opt-in:
# SUBSCRIBE DYN <rate> under Enable Level Meters. The amplifier caps the rate
# itself, per topic, and the cap matters: its per-connection send queue holds
# 64 messages and overflows ("#|E0: TXQueue Overflow - Messages dropped") for
# a client that cannot keep up. An overflow is written to Last Error and the
# driver reads the zone, output, input, mix and status values again.
#
# Rosters. Zones are letters (A-D in the document's table; the 1U manual says
# "A to H depending on amplifier output count"), outputs and route channels
# are numbers (route channel n is output n, document 1.4.6, so its registers
# live on the output). The amplifier reports how many of each it has:
# ZONE.COUNT fills the Zones setting and OUT.COUNT the Outputs setting, both
# saved once it connects. Inputs, mixes and wall volume controls depend on
# the model (Dante inputs on D models only, Mix 3-4 on four-channel models),
# so those rosters list every id the document defines and the amplifier's own
# GET <type>-*.NAME reply puts each one it has in service; the rest show as
# not fitted.
#
# Why YAML: one register per line with its own name on every value, so each
# register is one response rule and a push needs no different handling from
# a reply; the rosters are declarative; nothing needs code.

id: sonance_powerzone_connect
name: Sonance PowerZone Connect Amplifier
manufacturer: Sonance
category: audio
version: "1.0.1"
author: OpenAVC
transport: tcp
delimiter: "\n"
min_platform_version: "0.37.0"

description: >
  Controls Sonance PowerZone Connect (Blaze by Sonance) and PowerZone Connect
  PRO network DSP amplifiers over the Open API on TCP 7621. Each zone is a
  child entity with level, mute, source, stereo link, level limits, ducking
  and priority sources; each output has its name, level, mute, zone, delay
  and direct route; inputs and mixes carry their levels. Amplifier power,
  status, Dante status, wall volume controls and the test generator are
  covered too. State is pushed by the amplifier as it changes, including
  changes from its own web app and wall controllers.

source_url: https://images.salsify.com/images/vvbm6qkvqkj23mr6x4nq/Open%20API%20for%20Installers_Sonance_2026.24.1.pdf
tags: [amplifier, dsp, zone, background-music, 70v, 100v, dante, sonance, blaze, powerzone]
verified: false
simulated: true
protocols: [sonance_open_api]
ports: [7621]

compatible_models:
  - manufacturer: Sonance
    models:
      - PowerZone Connect PRO 300.2
      - PowerZone Connect PRO 300.2D
      - PowerZone Connect PRO 600.2
      - PowerZone Connect PRO 600.2D
      - PowerZone Connect PRO 600.4
      - PowerZone Connect PRO 600.4D
      - PowerZone Connect PRO 1200.4
      - PowerZone Connect PRO 1200.4D
      - PowerZone Connect PRO 2000.2
      - PowerZone Connect PRO 2000.2D
      - PowerZone Connect PRO 4000.4
      - PowerZone Connect PRO 4000.4D
    confidence: untested
    notes: >
      70 V / 100 V models (Lo-Z selectable), two or four channels. The PRO
      firmware is built on the PowerZone Connect platform and Sonance offers
      the same Open API for it. Built from the document; not yet run on a
      unit. Models ending in D have Dante: tick Dante Model.
  - manufacturer: Sonance
    models:
      - PowerZone Connect 122
      - PowerZone Connect 122D
      - PowerZone Connect 252
      - PowerZone Connect 254
      - PowerZone Connect 504
      - PowerZone Connect 504D
      - PowerZone Connect 1002
      - PowerZone Connect 1502
      - PowerZone Connect 2004
      - PowerZone Connect 2004D
      - PowerZone Connect 3004
      - PowerZone Connect 3004D
    confidence: untested
    notes: >
      Blaze by Sonance models (formerly Blaze Audio) with two or four outputs,
      zones A to D: the range the Open API document's tables define. Built
      from the document; not yet run on a unit. Models ending in D have
      Dante: tick Dante Model.
  - manufacturer: Sonance
    models:
      - PowerZone Connect 508
      - PowerZone Connect 1008
      - PowerZone Connect 1008D
      - PowerZone Connect 4008
      - PowerZone Connect 6008
      - PowerZone Connect 6008D
    confidence: untested
    notes: >
      Eight-output models. The Open API document's tables stop at zones A-D
      and outputs 1-4; the 1U manual names zones A to H by output count, and
      the driver addresses zones E-H and outputs 5-8 the same way once the
      amplifier reports eight. That addressing is not in the API document and
      has not been seen on a unit.

help:
  overview: >
    PowerZone Connect amplifiers are zoned background-music amplifiers with a
    built-in DSP: each zone picks a source (an analog, S/PDIF or Dante input,
    a mix, or the test generator) and has its own level, mute, level limits,
    ducking and priority sources; each output follows a zone. This driver
    makes every zone, output, input and mix its own entity, so a panel binds
    to "Zone B level" or "Zone A source" directly. The amplifier reports every
    change as it happens, so the panel stays right when staff use the wall
    controller, the Venue Control app or the web app.
  setup: >
    1. Give the amplifier a fixed address (a static IP or a DHCP reservation)
    in its web app. Out of the box it is 192.168.64.100.
    2. Enter that address. The control port is 7621 and needs no password:
    the API has no sign-in, so anything that reaches port 7621 can control
    the amplifier. Keep it on a protected network.
    3. Zones and outputs fill in by themselves once the amplifier connects,
    and the counts are saved in Zones and Outputs. Set them yourself only to
    build a project before the amplifier is reachable.
    4. Tick Dante Model for a model ending in D, so its Dante status is read.
    5. In an Eco Power On Mode the amplifier switches its network off while
    in standby, so it reads offline here until audio or a trigger wakes it.
    Choose a mode without Eco if it must stay controllable in standby.
    6. Leave Enable Level Meters off unless a panel shows live meters.

default_config:
  host: ""
  port: 7621
  poll_interval: 10
  inter_command_delay: 0
  zones: "A,B,C,D"
  output_count: "4"
  has_dante: false
  enable_meters: false
  meter_rate: 2
  tcp_keepalive: true

config_schema:
  host:
    type: string
    required: true
    default: ""
    label: "IP Address"
    description: "The amplifier's address (192.168.64.100 out of the box)."
  port:
    type: integer
    required: true
    default: 7621
    label: "Port"
    description: "Open API control port, 7621 on every model."
    min: 1
    max: 65535
  zones:
    type: string
    required: false
    default: "A,B,C,D"
    label: "Zones"
    learned_from: zone_ids
    description: >
      Zone letters, comma-separated: A,B for a two-channel model, A,B,C,D for
      four, A to H for eight. Once the amplifier connects, the zones it
      reports are saved here.
  output_count:
    type: enum
    required: false
    default: "4"
    label: "Outputs"
    learned_from: out_count
    description: >
      Amplifier outputs, the last digit of the model number (PRO 600.4 = 4,
      122 = 2, 1008 = 8). Once the amplifier connects, the count it reports
      is saved here.
    values:
      - { value: "1", label: "1 output" }
      - { value: "2", label: "2 outputs" }
      - { value: "4", label: "4 outputs" }
      - { value: "8", label: "8 outputs" }
  has_dante:
    type: boolean
    default: false
    label: "Dante Model"
    description: "Tick for a model ending in D, so its Dante status is read."
  enable_meters:
    type: boolean
    default: false
    label: "Enable Level Meters"
    description: >
      Stream live signal meters for every input, zone and output. Off unless a
      panel shows meters: it adds steady traffic.
  meter_rate:
    type: number
    default: 2
    label: "Meter Updates per Second"
    description: >
      How often the amplifier sends each meter while meters are on. It caps
      the rate itself; keep it low on a busy network.
    min: 0.1
    max: 20
  poll_interval:
    type: integer
    default: 10
    label: "Poll Interval (s)"
    description: "Changes are pushed by the amplifier; this re-reads its status and the wall controller levels."
    min: 0
    max: 3600

discovery:
  # The probe and the mDNS service identify the amplifier platform, not the
  # brand: the document's own examples come from the platform's maker (mDNS
  # manufacturer=Pascal Audio, VENDOR_NAME "Pascal", MODEL_NAME "BLAZE-4"),
  # so both are cross_vendor and the Sonance block below says whose it is.
  tcp_probe:
    port: 7621
    send_ascii: "GET SYSTEM.DEVICE.MODEL_NAME\n"
    expect_regex: '\+SYSTEM\.DEVICE\.MODEL_NAME "'
    cross_vendor: true
    extract:
      model:
        regex: '\+SYSTEM\.DEVICE\.MODEL_NAME "([^"]*)"'
        group: 1
    timeout_ms: 2000
  mdns:
    - service: "_pasconnect._tcp"
      cross_vendor: true
  # 40:11:DC is Sonance's own IEEE MA-L block. Pascal Audio's 88:02:64 is
  # left out on purpose: other brands' amplifiers on the same platform carry
  # it and would all be labelled Sonance.
  oui:
    - "40:11:dc"
  port_open:
    - 7621
  manufacturer_alias:
    - "sonance"
    - "blaze"
    - "blaze audio"
    - "blaze by sonance"

child_entity_types:
  zone:
    label: "Zone"
    label_plural: "Zones"
    id_format:
      type: string
      max_length: 1
    instances:
      # The letters the amplifier has, saved from ZONE.COUNT once it connects.
      ids_from: zones
      label: "Zone {id}"
    label_field: name
    summary_fields: ["name", "gain", "mute", "source_name"]
    state_variables:
      name:
        type: string
        label: "Zone Name"
      gain:
        type: number
        label: "Level (dB)"
        help: "Zone volume. The amplifier keeps it between the zone's Minimum and Maximum Level, and refuses it while a wall volume control is assigned."
        min: -80.0
        max: 0.0
        step: 0.5
        unit: "dB"
        control: true
        cloud_priority: high
      gain_min:
        type: number
        label: "Minimum Level (dB)"
        min: -80.0
        max: 0.0
        unit: "dB"
      gain_max:
        type: number
        label: "Maximum Level (dB)"
        min: -80.0
        max: 0.0
        unit: "dB"
      mute:
        type: boolean
        label: "Mute"
        control: true
        cloud_priority: high
      mute_enable:
        type: boolean
        label: "Mute Allowed"
        help: "When off, the zone cannot be muted (the amplifier answers E128: Mute disabled)."
      source:
        type: integer
        label: "Source"
        help: "The zone's primary source, as the amplifier numbers it (100 = Analog 1, 500 = Mix 1, 0 = none). Source Name has its name."
        control: true
        cloud_priority: high
      source_name:
        type: string
        label: "Source Name"
      stereo:
        type: boolean
        label: "Stereo"
        help: "On when this zone is linked with the next one as a stereo pair; the next zone is then inactive."
      gpio_vc:
        type: integer
        label: "Wall Volume Control"
        help: "Which wall volume control sets this zone's level (1-4, GPIO pins 4-7), or 0 for none. While one is assigned, the zone's level cannot be set from here."
        min: 0
        max: 4
      duck_mode:
        type: enum
        values: ["OFF", "DUCKER", "OVERRIDE"]
        label: "Ducking Mode"
        help: "OFF, DUCKER (a priority input lowers the primary source) or OVERRIDE (a priority input replaces it)."
      priority_2_source:
        type: integer
        label: "Priority 2 (Medium) Source"
        help: "Input that takes over the zone when it carries signal, above the primary source. Same numbering as Source."
      priority_3_source:
        type: integer
        label: "Priority 3 (Highest) Source"
        help: "Input that takes over the zone above every other, an alarm for example. Same numbering as Source."
      compressor_bypass:
        type: boolean
        label: "Compressor Bypassed"
      signal:
        type: number
        label: "Signal (dB)"
        help: "Live zone meter, only while Enable Level Meters is on."
        min: -144.0
        max: 20.0
        unit: "dB"
        cloud_priority: low
  output:
    label: "Output"
    label_plural: "Outputs"
    id_format:
      type: integer
      min: 1
      max: 8
    instances:
      count_from: output_count
      count_from_state: out_count
      label: "Output {id}"
    label_field: name
    summary_fields: ["name", "zone", "mute", "gain"]
    state_variables:
      name:
        type: string
        label: "Output Name"
      gain:
        type: number
        label: "Output Level (dB)"
        help: "Output trim after the zone level."
        min: -30.0
        max: 15.0
        step: 0.5
        unit: "dB"
        control: true
      mute:
        type: boolean
        label: "Mute"
        control: true
        cloud_priority: high
      zone:
        type: string
        label: "Zone"
        help: "The zone this output plays (its letter), empty when none."
        control: true
      channel:
        type: enum
        values: ["L", "R", "S"]
        label: "Channel"
        help: "Which side of the zone it plays: L (left), R (right) or S (left and right summed)."
      mode:
        type: enum
        values: ["OFF", "4R", "8R", "70V", "100V", "BTL"]
        label: "Output Mode"
        help: "OFF, 4R or 8R (low impedance), 70V or 100V (constant voltage), or BTL (bridged). Set in the amplifier's web app."
      delay:
        type: number
        label: "Delay (s)"
        min: 0.0
        max: 0.1
        unit: "s"
      delay_bypass:
        type: boolean
        label: "Delay Bypassed"
      eq_bypass:
        type: boolean
        label: "Output EQ Bypassed"
      preset_name:
        type: string
        label: "Speaker Preset"
        help: "The speaker preset loaded on this output (its EQ, crossover and limiters are set by the preset in the web app)."
      preset_locked:
        type: boolean
        label: "Speaker Preset Locked"
      route_source:
        type: integer
        label: "Route Source"
        help: "The document's direct output route (advanced use): an input, mix or zone number sent to this output (1000 = Zone A), 0 for none."
      route_channel:
        type: enum
        values: ["L", "R", "S"]
        label: "Route Channel"
      route_gain:
        type: number
        label: "Route Level (dB)"
        min: -40.0
        max: 20.0
        unit: "dB"
      signal:
        type: number
        label: "Signal (dB)"
        help: "Live output meter, only while Enable Level Meters is on."
        min: -144.0
        max: 20.0
        unit: "dB"
        cloud_priority: low
      clip:
        type: boolean
        label: "Clip"
        help: "Live clip indicator, only while Enable Level Meters is on."
        cloud_priority: low
      route_signal:
        type: number
        label: "Route Signal (dB)"
        min: -144.0
        max: 20.0
        unit: "dB"
        cloud_priority: low
      route_clip:
        type: boolean
        label: "Route Clip"
        cloud_priority: low
  input:
    label: "Input"
    label_plural: "Inputs"
    id_format:
      type: integer
      min: 100
      max: 400
    instances:
      # Every input the document defines. Which ones a unit has depends on the
      # model (Dante 300-303 on D models, Analog 5-8 on eight-input ones), and
      # the amplifier's answer to GET IN-*.NAME puts each one it has in service.
      ids: [100, 101, 102, 103, 104, 105, 106, 107, 200, 201, 300, 301, 302, 303, 400]
      presence: reported
      label: "Input {id}"
    label_field: name
    summary_fields: ["name", "gain", "sensitivity"]
    state_variables:
      name:
        type: string
        label: "Input Name"
      gain:
        type: number
        label: "Input Gain (dB)"
        help: "Input trim, -15 to +15 dB (the Noise Generator, input 400: -48 to 0 dB)."
        min: -48.0
        max: 15.0
        step: 0.5
        unit: "dB"
      sensitivity:
        type: enum
        values: ["14DBU", "4DBU", "-10DBV", "MIC"]
        label: "Sensitivity"
        help: "14DBU or 4DBU (professional line level), -10DBV (consumer line level) or MIC (dynamic microphone)."
      stereo:
        type: boolean
        label: "Stereo"
        help: "On when this input is linked with the next one as a stereo pair."
      hpf_enable:
        type: boolean
        label: "High Pass Filter"
      eq_bypass:
        type: boolean
        label: "Input EQ Bypassed"
      signal:
        type: number
        label: "Signal (dB)"
        help: "Live input meter, only while Enable Level Meters is on."
        min: -144.0
        max: 20.0
        unit: "dB"
        cloud_priority: low
      clip:
        type: boolean
        label: "Clip"
        cloud_priority: low
  mix:
    label: "Mix"
    label_plural: "Mixes"
    id_format:
      type: integer
      min: 1
      max: 4
    instances:
      # Mix 3 and 4 exist on four-channel models only (document 1.4.2); the
      # amplifier's answer to GET MIX-*.NAME puts each mix it has in service.
      ids: [1, 2, 3, 4]
      presence: reported
      label: "Mix {id}"
    label_field: name
    summary_fields: ["name"]
    state_variables:
      name:
        type: string
        label: "Mix Name"
      level_100:
        type: number
        label: "Analog 1 Level (dB)"
        min: -144.0
        max: 0.0
        unit: "dB"
      level_101:
        type: number
        label: "Analog 2 Level (dB)"
        min: -144.0
        max: 0.0
        unit: "dB"
      level_102:
        type: number
        label: "Analog 3 Level (dB)"
        min: -144.0
        max: 0.0
        unit: "dB"
      level_103:
        type: number
        label: "Analog 4 Level (dB)"
        min: -144.0
        max: 0.0
        unit: "dB"
      level_104:
        type: number
        label: "Analog 5 Level (dB)"
        min: -144.0
        max: 0.0
        unit: "dB"
      level_105:
        type: number
        label: "Analog 6 Level (dB)"
        min: -144.0
        max: 0.0
        unit: "dB"
      level_106:
        type: number
        label: "Analog 7 Level (dB)"
        min: -144.0
        max: 0.0
        unit: "dB"
      level_107:
        type: number
        label: "Analog 8 Level (dB)"
        min: -144.0
        max: 0.0
        unit: "dB"
      level_200:
        type: number
        label: "S/PDIF Left Level (dB)"
        min: -144.0
        max: 0.0
        unit: "dB"
      level_201:
        type: number
        label: "S/PDIF Right Level (dB)"
        min: -144.0
        max: 0.0
        unit: "dB"
      level_300:
        type: number
        label: "Dante 1 Level (dB)"
        min: -144.0
        max: 0.0
        unit: "dB"
      level_301:
        type: number
        label: "Dante 2 Level (dB)"
        min: -144.0
        max: 0.0
        unit: "dB"
      level_302:
        type: number
        label: "Dante 3 Level (dB)"
        min: -144.0
        max: 0.0
        unit: "dB"
      level_303:
        type: number
        label: "Dante 4 Level (dB)"
        min: -144.0
        max: 0.0
        unit: "dB"
      level_400:
        type: number
        label: "Noise Generator Level (dB)"
        min: -144.0
        max: 0.0
        unit: "dB"
  volume_control:
    label: "Wall Volume Control"
    label_plural: "Wall Volume Controls"
    id_format:
      type: integer
      min: 1
      max: 4
    instances:
      # Volume controls 1-4 are GPIO pins 4-7 (document 1.4.9); the answer to
      # GET VC-*.NAME puts each one the amplifier has in service.
      ids: [1, 2, 3, 4]
      presence: reported
      label: "Wall Volume Control {id}"
    label_field: name
    summary_fields: ["name", "value"]
    state_variables:
      name:
        type: string
        label: "Name"
      value:
        type: number
        label: "Position (%)"
        help: "Where the wall controller's knob sits, 0-100%."
        min: 0.0
        max: 100.0
        unit: "%"

state_variables:
  power:
    type: boolean
    label: "Power"
    help: "On when the amplifier reports ON; off in standby, forced standby or while it starts."
    control: true
    cloud_priority: high
  system_state:
    type: enum
    values: ["INIT", "STANDBY", "STANDBY_FORCED", "ON"]
    label: "Amplifier State"
    help: "INIT (starting), STANDBY, STANDBY_FORCED (protection or over-temperature) or ON."
    cloud_priority: high
  signal_in:
    type: enum
    values: ["OFF", "NO_SIGNAL", "SIGNAL", "CLIP"]
    label: "Input Signal"
    help: "OFF, NO_SIGNAL, SIGNAL or CLIP (an input is overloading: lower its sensitivity)."
    cloud_priority: high
  signal_out:
    type: enum
    values: ["OFF", "NO_SIGNAL", "SIGNAL", "CLIP", "FAULT"]
    label: "Output Signal"
    help: "OFF, NO_SIGNAL, SIGNAL, CLIP (an output is clipping: lower the volume) or FAULT."
    cloud_priority: high
  model_name:
    type: string
    label: "Model"
  vendor_name:
    type: string
    label: "Vendor"
  serial_number:
    type: string
    label: "Serial Number"
  firmware_version:
    type: string
    label: "Firmware Version"
  firmware_date:
    type: string
    label: "Firmware Date"
  api_version:
    type: string
    label: "API Version"
  hardware_id:
    type: integer
    label: "Hardware ID"
  software_id:
    type: integer
    label: "Software ID"
  mac_address:
    type: string
    label: "MAC Address"
  wifi_mac_address:
    type: string
    label: "Wi-Fi MAC Address"
  lan_status:
    type: string
    label: "LAN Address"
    help: "The amplifier's wired IP address, empty when the LAN is not connected."
  wifi_status:
    type: string
    label: "Wi-Fi Status"
  device_name:
    type: string
    label: "Device Name"
  venue_name:
    type: string
    label: "Venue Name"
  customer_name:
    type: string
    label: "Customer Name"
  installer_name:
    type: string
    label: "Installer Name"
  contact_info:
    type: string
    label: "Contact Info"
  install_date:
    type: string
    label: "Install Date"
  asset_tag:
    type: string
    label: "Asset Tag"
  locating:
    type: boolean
    label: "Locating"
    help: "On while the amplifier flashes its LEDs so it can be found in the rack."
  power_on_mode:
    type: enum
    values: ["AUDIO", "AUDIO_ECO", "AUDIO_DSP", "TRIGGER", "TRIGGER_ECO", "NETWORK"]
    label: "Power On Mode"
  mute_time:
    type: integer
    label: "Mute After No Signal (s)"
    min: 0
    max: 3600
    unit: "s"
  standby_time:
    type: integer
    label: "Standby After No Signal (s)"
    help: "0 = never."
    min: 0
    max: 3600
    unit: "s"
  generator_type:
    type: enum
    values: ["PINK", "SINE"]
    label: "Generator Type"
  sine_frequency:
    type: number
    label: "Sine Frequency (Hz)"
    min: 20.0
    max: 20000.0
    unit: "Hz"
  pink_lpf_enable:
    type: boolean
    label: "Pink Noise Low Pass"
  pink_lpf_frequency:
    type: number
    label: "Pink Noise Low Pass (Hz)"
    min: 20.0
    max: 20000.0
    unit: "Hz"
  pink_hpf_enable:
    type: boolean
    label: "Pink Noise High Pass"
  pink_hpf_frequency:
    type: number
    label: "Pink Noise High Pass (Hz)"
    min: 20.0
    max: 20000.0
    unit: "Hz"
  zone_count:
    type: integer
    label: "Zones Reported"
  zone_ids:
    type: string
    label: "Zone Letters Reported"
  out_count:
    type: integer
    label: "Outputs Reported"
  in_count:
    type: integer
    label: "Inputs Reported"
  mix_count:
    type: integer
    label: "Mixes Reported"
  vc_count:
    type: integer
    label: "Wall Volume Controls Reported"
  dante_device_name:
    type: string
    label: "Dante Device Name"
  dante_ip:
    type: string
    label: "Dante IP Address"
  dante_mac:
    type: string
    label: "Dante MAC Address"
  dante_firmware_version:
    type: string
    label: "Dante Firmware Version"
  dante_software_version:
    type: string
    label: "Dante Software Version"
  dante_link_speed:
    type: integer
    label: "Dante Link Speed"
  dante_aes67:
    type: boolean
    label: "AES67 Enabled"
  dante_encoding:
    type: enum
    values: ["PCM16", "PCM24", "PCM32"]
    label: "Dante Encoding"
  dante_sample_rate:
    type: enum
    values: ["44100", "48000", "96000"]
    label: "Dante Sample Rate"
  dante_clock_state:
    type: enum
    values: ["NO_CLOCK", "LOCKING", "LOCKED"]
    label: "Dante Clock"
    cloud_priority: high
  dante_mute_state:
    type: string
    label: "Dante Mute State"
  last_error:
    type: string
    label: "Last Error"
    help: "The amplifier's last refusal: the command, then its message (E126: Volume is controlled by GPIO volume control)."

device_settings:
  # Amplifier-wide values the amplifier keeps and reports back (each write is
  # echoed by the REG subscription). Per-zone and per-output values are child
  # state with commands instead: a setting's state key cannot name a child.
  device_name:
    type: string
    label: "Device Name"
    help: "The name the amplifier shows in its web app and on the network, up to 32 characters."
    default: ""
    regex: '^[^"]{1,32}$'
    state_key: "device_name"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: 'SET SETUP.SYSTEM.DEVICE_NAME "{value}"\n'
  venue_name:
    type: string
    label: "Venue Name"
    help: "Up to 32 characters."
    default: ""
    regex: '^[^"]{0,32}$'
    state_key: "venue_name"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: 'SET SETUP.SYSTEM.VENUE_NAME "{value}"\n'
  customer_name:
    type: string
    label: "Customer Name"
    help: "Up to 32 characters."
    default: ""
    regex: '^[^"]{0,32}$'
    state_key: "customer_name"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: 'SET SETUP.SYSTEM.CUSTOMER_NAME "{value}"\n'
  installer_name:
    type: string
    label: "Installer Name"
    help: "Up to 32 characters."
    default: ""
    regex: '^[^"]{0,32}$'
    state_key: "installer_name"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: 'SET SETUP.SYSTEM.INSTALLER_NAME "{value}"\n'
  contact_info:
    type: string
    label: "Contact Info"
    help: "Up to 32 characters."
    default: ""
    regex: '^[^"]{0,32}$'
    state_key: "contact_info"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: 'SET SETUP.SYSTEM.CONTACT_INFO "{value}"\n'
  install_date:
    type: string
    label: "Install Date"
    help: "Free text, up to 32 characters."
    default: ""
    regex: '^[^"]{0,32}$'
    state_key: "install_date"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: 'SET SETUP.SYSTEM.INSTALL_DATE "{value}"\n'
  asset_tag:
    type: string
    label: "Asset Tag"
    help: "Up to 32 characters."
    default: ""
    regex: '^[^"]{0,32}$'
    state_key: "asset_tag"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: 'SET SETUP.SYSTEM.ASSET_TAG "{value}"\n'
  locating:
    type: boolean
    label: "Locate"
    help: "Flashes the amplifier's LEDs so it can be found in the rack. Turn it off again when done."
    default: false
    state_key: "locating"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: "SET SETUP.SYSTEM.LOCATING {value:d}\n"
  power_on_mode:
    type: enum
    label: "Power On Mode"
    help: >
      What wakes the amplifier from standby: AUDIO (an input signal), AUDIO_DSP,
      TRIGGER (the 12 V trigger or a standby switch), NETWORK, or the ECO forms
      of AUDIO and TRIGGER, which switch the network off in standby so the
      amplifier is unreachable until it wakes. Power On and Power Off are
      accepted only in some modes.
    default: "AUDIO"
    values:
      - { value: "AUDIO", label: "Audio" }
      - { value: "AUDIO_ECO", label: "Audio (Eco: network off in standby)" }
      - { value: "AUDIO_DSP", label: "Audio (DSP)" }
      - { value: "TRIGGER", label: "Trigger" }
      - { value: "TRIGGER_ECO", label: "Trigger (Eco: network off in standby)" }
      - { value: "NETWORK", label: "Network" }
    state_key: "power_on_mode"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: "SET SETUP.POWER.POWER_ON {value}\n"
  mute_time:
    type: integer
    label: "Mute After No Signal (s)"
    help: "Seconds without an input signal before the outputs mute, 0 to 3600."
    default: 300
    min: 0
    max: 3600
    state_key: "mute_time"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: "SET SETUP.POWER.MUTE_TIME {value}\n"
  standby_time:
    type: integer
    label: "Standby After No Signal (s)"
    help: "Seconds without an input signal before the amplifier goes to standby, 0 to 3600 (0 = never)."
    default: 900
    min: 0
    max: 3600
    state_key: "standby_time"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: "SET SETUP.POWER.STANDBY_TIME {value}\n"
  generator_type:
    type: enum
    label: "Generator Type"
    help: "The test generator (input 400): pink noise or a sine tone."
    default: "PINK"
    values:
      - { value: "PINK", label: "Pink noise" }
      - { value: "SINE", label: "Sine tone" }
    state_key: "generator_type"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: "SET GENERATOR.TYPE {value}\n"
  sine_frequency:
    type: number
    label: "Sine Frequency (Hz)"
    help: "20 to 20000 Hz."
    default: 1000
    min: 20
    max: 20000
    state_key: "sine_frequency"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: "SET GENERATOR.SINE.FREQ {value}\n"
  pink_lpf_enable:
    type: boolean
    label: "Pink Noise Low Pass"
    default: false
    state_key: "pink_lpf_enable"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: "SET GENERATOR.PINK.LPF_ENABLE {value:d}\n"
  pink_lpf_frequency:
    type: number
    label: "Pink Noise Low Pass (Hz)"
    help: "20 to 20000 Hz."
    default: 20000
    min: 20
    max: 20000
    state_key: "pink_lpf_frequency"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: "SET GENERATOR.PINK.LPF_FREQ {value}\n"
  pink_hpf_enable:
    type: boolean
    label: "Pink Noise High Pass"
    default: false
    state_key: "pink_hpf_enable"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: "SET GENERATOR.PINK.HPF_ENABLE {value:d}\n"
  pink_hpf_frequency:
    type: number
    label: "Pink Noise High Pass (Hz)"
    help: "20 to 20000 Hz."
    default: 20
    min: 20
    max: 20000
    state_key: "pink_hpf_frequency"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: "SET GENERATOR.PINK.HPF_FREQ {value}\n"

commands:

  # ── Zones ──

  set_zone_level:
    label: "Set Zone Level"
    send: "SET ZONE-{zone}.GAIN {level}\n"
    sets: { gain: "{level}" }
    help: >
      Sets the zone's volume in dB (0 = full, -80 = lowest). The amplifier keeps
      it within the zone's Minimum and Maximum Level, and refuses it (into Last
      Error) while a wall volume control is assigned to the zone.
    params:
      zone:
        type: child_id
        child_type: zone
        required: true
        label: "Zone"
      level:
        type: number
        required: true
        label: "Level (dB)"
        min: -80.0
        max: 0.0
        decimals: 1

  zone_level_up:
    label: "Zone Level Up"
    send: "INC ZONE-{zone}.GAIN {step}\n"
    help: "Raises the zone's volume by the step, in dB; the amplifier answers with the new level."
    params:
      zone:
        type: child_id
        child_type: zone
        required: true
        label: "Zone"
      step:
        type: number
        required: true
        default: 1.0
        label: "Step (dB)"
        min: 0.5
        max: 20.0
        decimals: 1

  zone_level_down:
    label: "Zone Level Down"
    send: "INC ZONE-{zone}.GAIN -{step}\n"
    help: "Lowers the zone's volume by the step, in dB; the amplifier answers with the new level."
    params:
      zone:
        type: child_id
        child_type: zone
        required: true
        label: "Zone"
      step:
        type: number
        required: true
        default: 1.0
        label: "Step (dB)"
        min: 0.5
        max: 20.0
        decimals: 1

  mute_zone:
    label: "Mute Zone"
    send: "SET ZONE-{zone}.MUTE 1\n"
    sets: { mute: true }
    help: "Mutes the zone's speakers."
    params:
      zone:
        type: child_id
        child_type: zone
        required: true
        label: "Zone"

  unmute_zone:
    label: "Unmute Zone"
    send: "SET ZONE-{zone}.MUTE 0\n"
    sets: { mute: false }
    help: "Unmutes the zone's speakers."
    params:
      zone:
        type: child_id
        child_type: zone
        required: true
        label: "Zone"

  set_zone_source:
    label: "Set Zone Source"
    send: "SET ZONE-{zone}.PRIMARY_SRC {source}\n"
    sets: { source: "{source}" }
    help: >
      Picks what the zone plays. The list holds every source the family has:
      Dante sources exist on D models only, Mix 3 and 4 on four-channel models,
      and a source restricted for the zone in the web app is refused (E130:
      Source is Disabled). A refusal shows in Last Error.
    params:
      zone:
        type: child_id
        child_type: zone
        required: true
        label: "Zone"
      source:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: "Source"
        values:
          - { value: "0", label: "None (silent)" }
          - { value: "100", label: "Analog 1" }
          - { value: "101", label: "Analog 2" }
          - { value: "102", label: "Analog 3" }
          - { value: "103", label: "Analog 4" }
          - { value: "104", label: "Analog 5" }
          - { value: "105", label: "Analog 6" }
          - { value: "106", label: "Analog 7" }
          - { value: "107", label: "Analog 8" }
          - { value: "200", label: "S/PDIF Left" }
          - { value: "201", label: "S/PDIF Right" }
          - { value: "300", label: "Dante 1" }
          - { value: "301", label: "Dante 2" }
          - { value: "302", label: "Dante 3" }
          - { value: "303", label: "Dante 4" }
          - { value: "400", label: "Noise Generator" }
          - { value: "500", label: "Mix 1" }
          - { value: "501", label: "Mix 2" }
          - { value: "502", label: "Mix 3" }
          - { value: "503", label: "Mix 4" }

  set_zone_name:
    label: "Set Zone Name"
    send: 'SET ZONE-{zone}.NAME "{name}"\n'
    sets: { name: "{name}" }
    help: "Names the zone on the amplifier (Bar, Patio)."
    params:
      zone:
        type: child_id
        child_type: zone
        required: true
        label: "Zone"
      name:
        type: string
        required: true
        label: "Name"
        pattern: '^[^"]{1,32}$'
        help: "Up to 32 characters, no double quotes."

  set_zone_stereo:
    label: "Set Zone Stereo"
    send: "SET ZONE-{zone}.STEREO {stereo}\n"
    help: >
      Links the zone with the next one as a stereo pair, or splits the pair
      back into mono zones. While linked, the next zone is inactive.
    params:
      zone:
        type: child_id
        child_type: zone
        required: true
        label: "Zone"
      stereo:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: "Stereo"
        values:
          - { value: "1", label: "Stereo (linked with the next zone)" }
          - { value: "0", label: "Mono" }

  set_zone_min_level:
    label: "Set Zone Minimum Level"
    send: "SET ZONE-{zone}.GAIN_MIN {level}\n"
    sets: { gain_min: "{level}" }
    help: "Sets the lowest volume the zone can be turned down to, in dB. It cannot be above the Maximum Level."
    params:
      zone:
        type: child_id
        child_type: zone
        required: true
        label: "Zone"
      level:
        type: number
        required: true
        label: "Level (dB)"
        min: -80.0
        max: 0.0
        decimals: 1

  set_zone_max_level:
    label: "Set Zone Maximum Level"
    send: "SET ZONE-{zone}.GAIN_MAX {level}\n"
    sets: { gain_max: "{level}" }
    help: "Sets the loudest the zone can be turned up to, in dB. It cannot be below the Minimum Level."
    params:
      zone:
        type: child_id
        child_type: zone
        required: true
        label: "Zone"
      level:
        type: number
        required: true
        label: "Level (dB)"
        min: -80.0
        max: 0.0
        decimals: 1

  set_zone_mute_allowed:
    label: "Allow Zone Mute"
    send: "SET ZONE-{zone}.MUTE_ENABLE {allowed}\n"
    help: "Allows or prevents muting the zone (from here, the wall controller and the apps)."
    params:
      zone:
        type: child_id
        child_type: zone
        required: true
        label: "Zone"
      allowed:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: "Mute"
        values:
          - { value: "1", label: "Mute allowed" }
          - { value: "0", label: "Mute not allowed" }

  set_zone_ducking:
    label: "Set Zone Ducking Mode"
    send: "SET ZONE-{zone}.DUCK.MODE {mode}\n"
    sets: { duck_mode: "{mode}" }
    help: "Turns the zone's ducking off, or sets it to lower (Ducker) or replace (Override) the primary source while a priority input carries signal."
    params:
      zone:
        type: child_id
        child_type: zone
        required: true
        label: "Zone"
      mode:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: "Mode"
        values:
          - { value: "OFF", label: "Off" }
          - { value: "DUCKER", label: "Ducker (lower the source)" }
          - { value: "OVERRIDE", label: "Override (replace the source)" }

  set_zone_priority_source:
    label: "Set Zone Priority Source"
    send: "SET ZONE-{zone}.PRIORITY-{priority}.SRC {source}\n"
    help: >
      Picks the input that takes over the zone at priority 2 (medium, a paging
      microphone) or 3 (highest, an alarm) while it carries signal. Firmware
      1.8 and later.
    params:
      zone:
        type: child_id
        child_type: zone
        required: true
        label: "Zone"
      priority:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: "Priority"
        values:
          - { value: "2", label: "Priority 2 (medium)" }
          - { value: "3", label: "Priority 3 (highest)" }
      source:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: "Source"
        values:
          - { value: "0", label: "None (silent)" }
          - { value: "100", label: "Analog 1" }
          - { value: "101", label: "Analog 2" }
          - { value: "102", label: "Analog 3" }
          - { value: "103", label: "Analog 4" }
          - { value: "104", label: "Analog 5" }
          - { value: "105", label: "Analog 6" }
          - { value: "106", label: "Analog 7" }
          - { value: "107", label: "Analog 8" }
          - { value: "200", label: "S/PDIF Left" }
          - { value: "201", label: "S/PDIF Right" }
          - { value: "300", label: "Dante 1" }
          - { value: "301", label: "Dante 2" }
          - { value: "302", label: "Dante 3" }
          - { value: "303", label: "Dante 4" }
          - { value: "400", label: "Noise Generator" }
          - { value: "500", label: "Mix 1" }
          - { value: "501", label: "Mix 2" }
          - { value: "502", label: "Mix 3" }
          - { value: "503", label: "Mix 4" }

  set_zone_compressor:
    label: "Set Zone Compressor"
    send: "SET ZONE-{zone}.COMPRESSOR.BYPASS {bypass}\n"
    help: "Turns the zone's compressor on or bypasses it."
    params:
      zone:
        type: child_id
        child_type: zone
        required: true
        label: "Zone"
      bypass:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: "Compressor"
        values:
          - { value: "1", label: "Bypassed" }
          - { value: "0", label: "On" }

  # ── Outputs ──

  mute_output:
    label: "Mute Output"
    send: "SET OUT-{output}.MUTE 1\n"
    sets: { mute: true }
    help: "Mutes one amplifier output."
    params:
      output:
        type: child_id
        child_type: output
        required: true
        label: "Output"

  unmute_output:
    label: "Unmute Output"
    send: "SET OUT-{output}.MUTE 0\n"
    sets: { mute: false }
    help: "Unmutes one amplifier output."
    params:
      output:
        type: child_id
        child_type: output
        required: true
        label: "Output"

  set_output_level:
    label: "Set Output Level"
    send: "SET OUT-{output}.GAIN {level}\n"
    sets: { gain: "{level}" }
    help: "Sets an output's trim in dB, -30 to +15, after the zone level."
    params:
      output:
        type: child_id
        child_type: output
        required: true
        label: "Output"
      level:
        type: number
        required: true
        label: "Level (dB)"
        min: -30.0
        max: 15.0
        decimals: 1

  set_output_name:
    label: "Set Output Name"
    send: 'SET OUT-{output}.NAME "{name}"\n'
    sets: { name: "{name}" }
    help: "Names an output on the amplifier (Bar Left)."
    params:
      output:
        type: child_id
        child_type: output
        required: true
        label: "Output"
      name:
        type: string
        required: true
        label: "Name"
        pattern: '^[^"]{1,32}$'
        help: "Up to 32 characters, no double quotes."

  set_output_zone:
    label: "Set Output Zone"
    send: "SET OUT-{output}.SRC {zone}\n"
    sets: { zone: "{zone}" }
    help: "Picks which zone an output plays. A zone the model lacks is refused into Last Error."
    params:
      output:
        type: child_id
        child_type: output
        required: true
        label: "Output"
      zone:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: "Zone"
        values: [A, B, C, D, E, F, G, H]

  set_output_channel:
    label: "Set Output Channel"
    send: "SET OUT-{output}.SRC_CHANNEL {channel}\n"
    sets: { channel: "{channel}" }
    help: "Picks which side of its zone an output plays: left, right, or both summed."
    params:
      output:
        type: child_id
        child_type: output
        required: true
        label: "Output"
      channel:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
        values:
          - { value: "L", label: "Left" }
          - { value: "R", label: "Right" }
          - { value: "S", label: "Left + right (summed)" }

  set_output_delay:
    label: "Set Output Delay"
    send: "SET OUT-{output}.DELAY.TIME {seconds}\n"
    sets: { delay: "{seconds}" }
    help: "Delays an output, 0 to 0.1 s, to line up speakers at different distances."
    params:
      output:
        type: child_id
        child_type: output
        required: true
        label: "Output"
      seconds:
        type: number
        required: true
        label: "Delay (s)"
        min: 0.0
        max: 0.1
        decimals: 4

  set_output_delay_bypass:
    label: "Set Output Delay Bypass"
    send: "SET OUT-{output}.DELAY.BYPASS {bypass}\n"
    help: "Bypasses an output's delay, or puts it back in."
    params:
      output:
        type: child_id
        child_type: output
        required: true
        label: "Output"
      bypass:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: "Delay"
        values:
          - { value: "1", label: "Bypassed" }
          - { value: "0", label: "On" }

  set_output_eq_bypass:
    label: "Set Output EQ Bypass"
    send: "SET OUT-{output}.EQ.BYPASS {bypass}\n"
    help: "Bypasses an output's room EQ, or puts it back in."
    params:
      output:
        type: child_id
        child_type: output
        required: true
        label: "Output"
      bypass:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: "Output EQ"
        values:
          - { value: "1", label: "Bypassed" }
          - { value: "0", label: "On" }

  set_output_route_source:
    label: "Set Output Route Source"
    send: "SET ROUT-{output}.SRC {source}\n"
    sets: { route_source: "{source}" }
    help: "Sends an input, a mix or a zone straight to an output (the document's direct route, advanced use)."
    params:
      output:
        type: child_id
        child_type: output
        required: true
        label: "Output"
      source:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: "Source"
        values:
          - { value: "0", label: "None (silent)" }
          - { value: "100", label: "Analog 1" }
          - { value: "101", label: "Analog 2" }
          - { value: "102", label: "Analog 3" }
          - { value: "103", label: "Analog 4" }
          - { value: "200", label: "S/PDIF Left" }
          - { value: "201", label: "S/PDIF Right" }
          - { value: "300", label: "Dante 1" }
          - { value: "301", label: "Dante 2" }
          - { value: "302", label: "Dante 3" }
          - { value: "303", label: "Dante 4" }
          - { value: "500", label: "Mix 1" }
          - { value: "501", label: "Mix 2" }
          - { value: "502", label: "Mix 3" }
          - { value: "503", label: "Mix 4" }
          - { value: "1000", label: "Zone A" }
          - { value: "1001", label: "Zone B" }
          - { value: "1002", label: "Zone C" }
          - { value: "1003", label: "Zone D" }

  set_output_route_channel:
    label: "Set Output Route Channel"
    send: "SET ROUT-{output}.SRC_CHANNEL {channel}\n"
    sets: { route_channel: "{channel}" }
    help: "Picks which side of the routed source an output's direct route carries."
    params:
      output:
        type: child_id
        child_type: output
        required: true
        label: "Output"
      channel:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
        values:
          - { value: "L", label: "Left" }
          - { value: "R", label: "Right" }
          - { value: "S", label: "Left + right (summed)" }

  set_output_route_level:
    label: "Set Output Route Level"
    send: "SET ROUT-{output}.GAIN {level}\n"
    sets: { route_gain: "{level}" }
    help: "Sets the level of an output's direct route, -40 to +20 dB."
    params:
      output:
        type: child_id
        child_type: output
        required: true
        label: "Output"
      level:
        type: number
        required: true
        label: "Level (dB)"
        min: -40.0
        max: 20.0
        decimals: 1

  # ── Inputs and mixes ──

  set_input_level:
    label: "Set Input Gain"
    send: "SET IN-{input}.GAIN {level}\n"
    sets: { gain: "{level}" }
    help: "Sets an input's trim in dB, -15 to +15 (the Noise Generator, input 400: -48 to 0)."
    params:
      input:
        type: child_id
        child_type: input
        required: true
        label: "Input"
      level:
        type: number
        required: true
        label: "Gain (dB)"
        min: -48.0
        max: 15.0
        decimals: 1

  set_input_name:
    label: "Set Input Name"
    send: 'SET IN-{input}.NAME "{name}"\n'
    sets: { name: "{name}" }
    help: "Names an input on the amplifier (Music, Paging Mic)."
    params:
      input:
        type: child_id
        child_type: input
        required: true
        label: "Input"
      name:
        type: string
        required: true
        label: "Name"
        pattern: '^[^"]{1,32}$'
        help: "Up to 32 characters, no double quotes."

  set_input_sensitivity:
    label: "Set Input Sensitivity"
    send: "SET IN-{input}.SENS {sensitivity}\n"
    sets: { sensitivity: "{sensitivity}" }
    help: "Matches an analog input to what is plugged in: professional line level, consumer line level, or a dynamic microphone."
    params:
      input:
        type: child_id
        child_type: input
        required: true
        label: "Input"
      sensitivity:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: "Sensitivity"
        values:
          - { value: "14DBU", label: "+14 dBu (professional)" }
          - { value: "4DBU", label: "+4 dBu (professional)" }
          - { value: "-10DBV", label: "-10 dBV (consumer)" }
          - { value: "MIC", label: "Microphone" }

  set_mix_level:
    label: "Set Mix Level"
    send: "SET MIX-{mix}.GAIN-{input} {level}\n"
    help: "Sets how much of one input goes into a mix, in dB (0 = full, -144 = none)."
    params:
      mix:
        type: child_id
        child_type: mix
        required: true
        label: "Mix"
      input:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: "Input"
        values:
          - { value: "100", label: "Analog 1" }
          - { value: "101", label: "Analog 2" }
          - { value: "102", label: "Analog 3" }
          - { value: "103", label: "Analog 4" }
          - { value: "104", label: "Analog 5" }
          - { value: "105", label: "Analog 6" }
          - { value: "106", label: "Analog 7" }
          - { value: "107", label: "Analog 8" }
          - { value: "200", label: "S/PDIF Left" }
          - { value: "201", label: "S/PDIF Right" }
          - { value: "300", label: "Dante 1" }
          - { value: "301", label: "Dante 2" }
          - { value: "302", label: "Dante 3" }
          - { value: "303", label: "Dante 4" }
          - { value: "400", label: "Noise Generator" }
      level:
        type: number
        required: true
        label: "Level (dB)"
        min: -144.0
        max: 0.0
        decimals: 1

  set_mix_name:
    label: "Set Mix Name"
    send: 'SET MIX-{mix}.NAME "{name}"\n'
    sets: { name: "{name}" }
    help: "Names a mix on the amplifier."
    params:
      mix:
        type: child_id
        child_type: mix
        required: true
        label: "Mix"
      name:
        type: string
        required: true
        label: "Name"
        pattern: '^[^"]{1,32}$'
        help: "Up to 32 characters, no double quotes."

  # ── Amplifier ──

  power_on:
    label: "Power On"
    send: "POWER_ON\n"
    help: >
      Wakes the amplifier from standby. It is accepted only in some Power On
      Modes; otherwise the amplifier answers E122 into Last Error.
    # No read-back in the send: the state passes through INIT on the way up,
    # and the 10 s poll reads SYSTEM.STATUS.STATE.

  power_off:
    label: "Power Off (Standby)"
    send: "POWER_OFF\n"
    help: >
      Puts the amplifier in standby: every zone goes silent. Accepted only in
      some Power On Modes (E122 into Last Error otherwise). In an Eco mode the
      amplifier also switches its network off, so it reads offline here until
      audio or a trigger wakes it.

  reboot:
    label: "Restart Amplifier"
    send: "REBOOT\n"
    confirm: "Restarts the amplifier. Audio stops in every zone until it is back."
    help: "Restarts the amplifier about a second after acknowledging. It goes offline here until it is back."

  factory_defaults:
    label: "Reset to Factory Defaults"
    send: "FACTORY_DEFAULTS\n"
    confirm: >
      Erases the amplifier's whole setup (zones, sources, names, speaker
      presets and power settings) and resets Dante. Every other control
      connection is closed.
    help: "Returns every setting on the amplifier to factory values and resets Dante."

quick_actions: [mute_zone, unmute_zone, set_zone_level, set_zone_source]

routing:
  # A zone picks its source and an output picks its zone. The direct output
  # route (ROUT) is advanced use and left off the matrix.
  planes:
    - label: "Zone Source"
      destination_child_type: zone
      route_property: source
      command: set_zone_source
    - label: "Output Zone"
      destination_child_type: output
      source_child_type: zone
      route_property: zone
      command: set_output_zone
      # Named: a parameter called zone otherwise reads as the destination.
      destination_param: output
      source_param: zone

responses:
  # Every value line is "+<register> <value>", from a GET, an INC or a push,
  # so one rule per register reads all three. Each rule names its register
  # up to the space before the value, so GAIN never reads GAIN_MIN.

  # ── Zones ──
  - match: '^\+ZONE-([A-H])\.NAME "(.*)"$'
    child_set:
      - { type: zone, id: $1, state: { name: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+ZONE-([A-H])\.GAIN (-?\d+(?:\.\d+)?)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: zone, id: $1, state: { gain: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+ZONE-([A-H])\.GAIN_MIN (-?\d+(?:\.\d+)?)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: zone, id: $1, state: { gain_min: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+ZONE-([A-H])\.GAIN_MAX (-?\d+(?:\.\d+)?)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: zone, id: $1, state: { gain_max: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+ZONE-([A-H])\.MUTE ([01])$'
    child_set:
      - { type: zone, id: $1, state: { mute: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+ZONE-([A-H])\.MUTE_ENABLE ([01])$'
    child_set:
      - { type: zone, id: $1, state: { mute_enable: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+ZONE-([A-H])\.PRIMARY_SRC (\d+)$'
    child_set:
      - type: zone
        id: $1
        state:
          source: $2
          source_name:
            group: 2
            map:
              "0": "None (silent)"
              "100": "Analog 1"
              "101": "Analog 2"
              "102": "Analog 3"
              "103": "Analog 4"
              "104": "Analog 5"
              "105": "Analog 6"
              "106": "Analog 7"
              "107": "Analog 8"
              "200": "S/PDIF Left"
              "201": "S/PDIF Right"
              "300": "Dante 1"
              "301": "Dante 2"
              "302": "Dante 3"
              "303": "Dante 4"
              "400": "Noise Generator"
              "500": "Mix 1"
              "501": "Mix 2"
              "502": "Mix 3"
              "503": "Mix 4"

  - match: '^\+ZONE-([A-H])\.STEREO ([01])$'
    child_set:
      - { type: zone, id: $1, state: { stereo: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+ZONE-([A-H])\.GPIO_VC (\d+)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: zone, id: $1, state: { gpio_vc: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+ZONE-([A-H])\.DUCK\.MODE (OFF|DUCKER|OVERRIDE)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: zone, id: $1, state: { duck_mode: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+ZONE-([A-H])\.PRIORITY-2\.SRC (\d+)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: zone, id: $1, state: { priority_2_source: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+ZONE-([A-H])\.PRIORITY-3\.SRC (\d+)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: zone, id: $1, state: { priority_3_source: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+ZONE-([A-H])\.COMPRESSOR\.BYPASS ([01])$'
    child_set:
      - { type: zone, id: $1, state: { compressor_bypass: $2 } }

  # ── Outputs (OUT-n, and ROUT-n: route channel n is output n) ──
  - match: '^\+OUT-(\d+)\.NAME "(.*)"$'
    child_set:
      - { type: output, id: $1, state: { name: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+OUT-(\d+)\.GAIN (-?\d+(?:\.\d+)?)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: output, id: $1, state: { gain: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+OUT-(\d+)\.MUTE ([01])$'
    child_set:
      - { type: output, id: $1, state: { mute: $2 } }

  # OUT-n.SRC is a one-character string, so it may come back quoted ("A",
  # or "" for none) like every string, or bare: both are read.
  - match: '^\+OUT-(\d+)\.SRC "?([A-H]?)"?$'
    child_set:
      - { type: output, id: $1, state: { zone: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+OUT-(\d+)\.SRC_CHANNEL (L|R|S)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: output, id: $1, state: { channel: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+OUT-(\d+)\.OUTPUT_MODE (OFF|4R|8R|70V|100V|BTL)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: output, id: $1, state: { mode: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+OUT-(\d+)\.DELAY\.TIME (-?\d+(?:\.\d+)?)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: output, id: $1, state: { delay: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+OUT-(\d+)\.DELAY\.BYPASS ([01])$'
    child_set:
      - { type: output, id: $1, state: { delay_bypass: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+OUT-(\d+)\.EQ\.BYPASS ([01])$'
    child_set:
      - { type: output, id: $1, state: { eq_bypass: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+OUT-(\d+)\.PRESET\.NAME "(.*)"$'
    child_set:
      - { type: output, id: $1, state: { preset_name: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+OUT-(\d+)\.PRESET\.LOCKED ([01])$'
    child_set:
      - { type: output, id: $1, state: { preset_locked: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+ROUT-(\d+)\.SRC (\d+)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: output, id: $1, state: { route_source: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+ROUT-(\d+)\.SRC_CHANNEL (L|R|S)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: output, id: $1, state: { route_channel: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+ROUT-(\d+)\.GAIN (-?\d+(?:\.\d+)?)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: output, id: $1, state: { route_gain: $2 } }

  # ── Inputs: a name puts the input in service (a reported roster) ──
  - match: '^\+IN-(\d+)\.NAME "(.*)"$'
    child_set:
      - type: input
        id: $1
        state:
          name: $2
          online: "true"
          offline_reason: ""
          offline_detail: ""

  - match: '^\+IN-(\d+)\.GAIN (-?\d+(?:\.\d+)?)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: input, id: $1, state: { gain: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+IN-(\d+)\.SENS (14DBU|4DBU|-10DBV|MIC)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: input, id: $1, state: { sensitivity: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+IN-(\d+)\.STEREO ([01])$'
    child_set:
      - { type: input, id: $1, state: { stereo: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+IN-(\d+)\.HPF_ENABLE ([01])$'
    child_set:
      - { type: input, id: $1, state: { hpf_enable: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+IN-(\d+)\.EQ\.BYPASS ([01])$'
    child_set:
      - { type: input, id: $1, state: { eq_bypass: $2 } }

  # ── Mixes: a name puts the mix in service; one rule per input level ──
  - match: '^\+MIX-(\d+)\.NAME "(.*)"$'
    child_set:
      - type: mix
        id: $1
        state:
          name: $2
          online: "true"
          offline_reason: ""
          offline_detail: ""

  - match: '^\+MIX-(\d+)\.GAIN-100 (-?\d+(?:\.\d+)?)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: mix, id: $1, state: { level_100: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+MIX-(\d+)\.GAIN-101 (-?\d+(?:\.\d+)?)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: mix, id: $1, state: { level_101: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+MIX-(\d+)\.GAIN-102 (-?\d+(?:\.\d+)?)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: mix, id: $1, state: { level_102: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+MIX-(\d+)\.GAIN-103 (-?\d+(?:\.\d+)?)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: mix, id: $1, state: { level_103: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+MIX-(\d+)\.GAIN-104 (-?\d+(?:\.\d+)?)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: mix, id: $1, state: { level_104: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+MIX-(\d+)\.GAIN-105 (-?\d+(?:\.\d+)?)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: mix, id: $1, state: { level_105: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+MIX-(\d+)\.GAIN-106 (-?\d+(?:\.\d+)?)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: mix, id: $1, state: { level_106: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+MIX-(\d+)\.GAIN-107 (-?\d+(?:\.\d+)?)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: mix, id: $1, state: { level_107: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+MIX-(\d+)\.GAIN-200 (-?\d+(?:\.\d+)?)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: mix, id: $1, state: { level_200: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+MIX-(\d+)\.GAIN-201 (-?\d+(?:\.\d+)?)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: mix, id: $1, state: { level_201: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+MIX-(\d+)\.GAIN-300 (-?\d+(?:\.\d+)?)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: mix, id: $1, state: { level_300: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+MIX-(\d+)\.GAIN-301 (-?\d+(?:\.\d+)?)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: mix, id: $1, state: { level_301: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+MIX-(\d+)\.GAIN-302 (-?\d+(?:\.\d+)?)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: mix, id: $1, state: { level_302: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+MIX-(\d+)\.GAIN-303 (-?\d+(?:\.\d+)?)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: mix, id: $1, state: { level_303: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+MIX-(\d+)\.GAIN-400 (-?\d+(?:\.\d+)?)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: mix, id: $1, state: { level_400: $2 } }

  # ── Wall volume controls ──
  - match: '^\+VC-(\d+)\.NAME "(.*)"$'
    child_set:
      - type: volume_control
        id: $1
        state:
          name: $2
          online: "true"
          offline_reason: ""
          offline_detail: ""

  - match: '^\+VC-(\d+)\.VALUE (-?\d+(?:\.\d+)?)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: volume_control, id: $1, state: { value: $2 } }

  # ── Meters (SUBSCRIBE DYN, only while Enable Level Meters is on) ──
  # The amplifier already caps the rate at Meter Updates per Second; the
  # throttle (per child) only bounds a burst.
  - match: '^\+IN-(\d+)\.DYN\.SIGNAL (-?\d+(?:\.\d+)?)$'
    throttle: 0.25
    child_set:
      - { type: input, id: $1, state: { signal: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+IN-(\d+)\.DYN\.CLIP ([01])$'
    throttle: 0.25
    child_set:
      - { type: input, id: $1, state: { clip: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+ZONE-([A-H])\.DYN\.SIGNAL (-?\d+(?:\.\d+)?)$'
    throttle: 0.25
    child_set:
      - { type: zone, id: $1, state: { signal: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+OUT-(\d+)\.DYN\.SIGNAL (-?\d+(?:\.\d+)?)$'
    throttle: 0.25
    child_set:
      - { type: output, id: $1, state: { signal: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+OUT-(\d+)\.DYN\.CLIP ([01])$'
    throttle: 0.25
    child_set:
      - { type: output, id: $1, state: { clip: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+ROUT-(\d+)\.DYN\.SIGNAL (-?\d+(?:\.\d+)?)$'
    throttle: 0.25
    child_set:
      - { type: output, id: $1, state: { route_signal: $2 } }

  - match: '^\+ROUT-(\d+)\.DYN\.CLIP ([01])$'
    throttle: 0.25
    child_set:
      - { type: output, id: $1, state: { route_clip: $2 } }

  # ── Amplifier status ──
  - match: '^\+SYSTEM\.STATUS\.STATE (INIT|STANDBY|STANDBY_FORCED|ON)$'
    mappings:
      - { group: 1, state: system_state }
      - { group: 1, state: power, map: { "ON": "true", "STANDBY": "false", "STANDBY_FORCED": "false", "INIT": "false" } }

  - match: '^\+SYSTEM\.STATUS\.SIGNAL_IN (OFF|NO_SIGNAL|SIGNAL|CLIP)$'
    set: { signal_in: $1 }

  - match: '^\+SYSTEM\.STATUS\.SIGNAL_OUT (OFF|NO_SIGNAL|SIGNAL|CLIP|FAULT)$'
    set: { signal_out: $1 }

  - match: '^\+SYSTEM\.STATUS\.LAN "(.*)"$'
    set: { lan_status: $1 }

  - match: '^\+SYSTEM\.STATUS\.WIFI "(.*)"$'
    set: { wifi_status: $1 }

  # ── Identity ──
  - match: '^\+API_VERSION "(.*)"$'
    set: { api_version: $1 }

  - match: '^\+SYSTEM\.DEVICE\.VENDOR_NAME "(.*)"$'
    set: { vendor_name: $1 }

  - match: '^\+SYSTEM\.DEVICE\.MODEL_NAME "(.*)"$'
    set: { model_name: $1 }

  - match: '^\+SYSTEM\.DEVICE\.SERIAL "(.*)"$'
    set: { serial_number: $1 }

  - match: '^\+SYSTEM\.DEVICE\.FIRMWARE "(.*)"$'
    set: { firmware_version: $1 }

  - match: '^\+SYSTEM\.DEVICE\.FIRMWARE_DATE "(.*)"$'
    set: { firmware_date: $1 }

  - match: '^\+SYSTEM\.DEVICE\.MAC "(.*)"$'
    set: { mac_address: $1 }

  - match: '^\+SYSTEM\.DEVICE\.WIFI_MAC "(.*)"$'
    set: { wifi_mac_address: $1 }

  - match: '^\+SYSTEM\.DEVICE\.HWID (\d+)$'
    set: { hardware_id: $1 }

  - match: '^\+SYSTEM\.DEVICE\.SWID (\d+)$'
    set: { software_id: $1 }

  # ── Setup values (the device settings read back) ──
  - match: '^\+SETUP\.SYSTEM\.DEVICE_NAME "(.*)"$'
    set: { device_name: $1 }

  - match: '^\+SETUP\.SYSTEM\.VENUE_NAME "(.*)"$'
    set: { venue_name: $1 }

  - match: '^\+SETUP\.SYSTEM\.CUSTOMER_NAME "(.*)"$'
    set: { customer_name: $1 }

  - match: '^\+SETUP\.SYSTEM\.INSTALLER_NAME "(.*)"$'
    set: { installer_name: $1 }

  - match: '^\+SETUP\.SYSTEM\.CONTACT_INFO "(.*)"$'
    set: { contact_info: $1 }

  - match: '^\+SETUP\.SYSTEM\.INSTALL_DATE "(.*)"$'
    set: { install_date: $1 }

  - match: '^\+SETUP\.SYSTEM\.ASSET_TAG "(.*)"$'
    set: { asset_tag: $1 }

  - match: '^\+SETUP\.SYSTEM\.LOCATING ([01])$'
    set: { locating: $1 }

  - match: '^\+SETUP\.POWER\.POWER_ON (AUDIO|AUDIO_ECO|AUDIO_DSP|TRIGGER|TRIGGER_ECO|NETWORK)$'
    set: { power_on_mode: $1 }

  - match: '^\+SETUP\.POWER\.MUTE_TIME (\d+)$'
    set: { mute_time: $1 }

  - match: '^\+SETUP\.POWER\.STANDBY_TIME (\d+)$'
    set: { standby_time: $1 }

  - match: '^\+GENERATOR\.TYPE (PINK|SINE)$'
    set: { generator_type: $1 }

  - match: '^\+GENERATOR\.SINE\.FREQ (-?\d+(?:\.\d+)?)$'
    set: { sine_frequency: $1 }

  - match: '^\+GENERATOR\.PINK\.LPF_ENABLE ([01])$'
    set: { pink_lpf_enable: $1 }

  - match: '^\+GENERATOR\.PINK\.LPF_FREQ (-?\d+(?:\.\d+)?)$'
    set: { pink_lpf_frequency: $1 }

  - match: '^\+GENERATOR\.PINK\.HPF_ENABLE ([01])$'
    set: { pink_hpf_enable: $1 }

  - match: '^\+GENERATOR\.PINK\.HPF_FREQ (-?\d+(?:\.\d+)?)$'
    set: { pink_hpf_frequency: $1 }

  # ── Counts: the roster sizes ──
  # ZONE.COUNT names the zones as letters for the Zones setting (learned_from).
  - match: '^\+ZONE\.COUNT ([1-8])$'
    mappings:
      - { group: 1, state: zone_count }
      - { group: 1, state: zone_ids, map: { "1": "A", "2": "A,B", "3": "A,B,C", "4": "A,B,C,D", "5": "A,B,C,D,E", "6": "A,B,C,D,E,F", "7": "A,B,C,D,E,F,G", "8": "A,B,C,D,E,F,G,H" } }

  - match: '^\+OUT\.COUNT (\d+)$'
    set: { out_count: $1 }

  - match: '^\+IN\.COUNT (\d+)$'
    set: { in_count: $1 }

  - match: '^\+MIX\.COUNT (\d+)$'
    set: { mix_count: $1 }

  - match: '^\+VC\.COUNT (\d+)$'
    set: { vc_count: $1 }

  # ── Dante (D models, read only with Dante Model ticked) ──
  - match: '^\+SYSTEM\.DANTE\.DEVICE_NAME "(.*)"$'
    set: { dante_device_name: $1 }

  - match: '^\+SYSTEM\.DANTE\.IP "(.*)"$'
    set: { dante_ip: $1 }

  - match: '^\+SYSTEM\.DANTE\.MAC "(.*)"$'
    set: { dante_mac: $1 }

  - match: '^\+SYSTEM\.DANTE\.FIRMWARE_VERSION "(.*)"$'
    set: { dante_firmware_version: $1 }

  - match: '^\+SYSTEM\.DANTE\.SOFTWARE_VERSION "(.*)"$'
    set: { dante_software_version: $1 }

  - match: '^\+SYSTEM\.DANTE\.MUTE_STATE "(.*)"$'
    set: { dante_mute_state: $1 }

  - match: '^\+SYSTEM\.DANTE\.LINK_SPEED (\d+)$'
    set: { dante_link_speed: $1 }

  - match: '^\+SYSTEM\.DANTE\.AES67_ENABLED ([01])$'
    set: { dante_aes67: $1 }

  - match: '^\+SYSTEM\.DANTE\.ENCODING (PCM16|PCM24|PCM32)$'
    set: { dante_encoding: $1 }

  - match: '^\+SYSTEM\.DANTE\.SAMPLE_RATE (44100|48000|96000)$'
    set: { dante_sample_rate: $1 }

  - match: '^\+SYSTEM\.DANTE\.CLOCK_STATE (NO_CLOCK|LOCKING|LOCKED)$'
    set: { dante_clock_state: $1 }

  # ── Refusals, acknowledgements and the keep-alive ──
  # The send queue overflowed and pushes were dropped (document 4.1): say so
  # and read the values that change in use again, since any may be stale.
  - match: '^#\|(E0:.*)$'
    set: { last_error: $1 }
    then_query:
      - "GET ZONE-*.NAME\n"
      - "GET ZONE-*.GAIN\n"
      - "GET ZONE-*.GAIN_MIN\n"
      - "GET ZONE-*.GAIN_MAX\n"
      - "GET ZONE-*.MUTE\n"
      - "GET ZONE-*.MUTE_ENABLE\n"
      - "GET ZONE-*.PRIMARY_SRC\n"
      - "GET ZONE-*.STEREO\n"
      - "GET ZONE-*.GPIO_VC\n"
      - "GET ZONE-*.DUCK.MODE\n"
      - "GET ZONE-*.PRIORITY-2.SRC\n"
      - "GET ZONE-*.PRIORITY-3.SRC\n"
      - "GET ZONE-*.COMPRESSOR.BYPASS\n"
      - "GET OUT-*.GAIN\n"
      - "GET OUT-*.MUTE\n"
      - "GET OUT-*.SRC\n"
      - "GET OUT-*.SRC_CHANNEL\n"
      - "GET OUT-*.DELAY.TIME\n"
      - "GET OUT-*.DELAY.BYPASS\n"
      - "GET OUT-*.EQ.BYPASS\n"
      - "GET ROUT-*.SRC\n"
      - "GET ROUT-*.SRC_CHANNEL\n"
      - "GET ROUT-*.GAIN\n"
      - "GET IN-*.GAIN\n"
      - "GET IN-*.SENS\n"
      - "GET MIX-*.GAIN-100\n"
      - "GET MIX-*.GAIN-101\n"
      - "GET MIX-*.GAIN-102\n"
      - "GET MIX-*.GAIN-103\n"
      - "GET MIX-*.GAIN-104\n"
      - "GET MIX-*.GAIN-105\n"
      - "GET MIX-*.GAIN-106\n"
      - "GET MIX-*.GAIN-107\n"
      - "GET MIX-*.GAIN-200\n"
      - "GET MIX-*.GAIN-201\n"
      - "GET MIX-*.GAIN-300\n"
      - "GET MIX-*.GAIN-301\n"
      - "GET MIX-*.GAIN-302\n"
      - "GET MIX-*.GAIN-303\n"
      - "GET MIX-*.GAIN-400\n"
      - "GET SYSTEM.STATUS.STATE\n"
      - "GET SYSTEM.STATUS.SIGNAL_IN\n"
      - "GET SYSTEM.STATUS.SIGNAL_OUT\n"
      - "GET VC-*.VALUE\n"

  # #<command>|<message>: the whole line after the #, so Last Error names the
  # command the amplifier refused as well as why.
  - match: '^#(.+)$'
    set: { last_error: $1 }

  # *<command>: the command worked. Its value, if any, came before it.
  - match: '^\*.*$'
    set: {}

  - match: '^PONG$'
    set: {}

on_connect:
  # REG first: a SET is echoed only to a subscriber, and every change after
  # this line arrives on the connection. Then the initial read (the document
  # does not say a subscription replays current values): the counts first,
  # so the rosters are the amplifier's own before its values arrive.
  - "SUBSCRIBE REG\n"
  - { send: "SUBSCRIBE DYN {meter_rate}\n", when: enable_meters }
  - "GET ZONE.COUNT\n"
  - "GET OUT.COUNT\n"
  - "GET IN.COUNT\n"
  - "GET MIX.COUNT\n"
  - "GET VC.COUNT\n"
  - "GET ZONE-*.NAME\n"
  - "GET ZONE-*.GAIN\n"
  - "GET ZONE-*.GAIN_MIN\n"
  - "GET ZONE-*.GAIN_MAX\n"
  - "GET ZONE-*.MUTE\n"
  - "GET ZONE-*.MUTE_ENABLE\n"
  - "GET ZONE-*.PRIMARY_SRC\n"
  - "GET ZONE-*.STEREO\n"
  - "GET ZONE-*.GPIO_VC\n"
  - "GET ZONE-*.DUCK.MODE\n"
  - "GET ZONE-*.PRIORITY-2.SRC\n"
  - "GET ZONE-*.PRIORITY-3.SRC\n"
  - "GET ZONE-*.COMPRESSOR.BYPASS\n"
  - "GET OUT-*.NAME\n"
  - "GET OUT-*.GAIN\n"
  - "GET OUT-*.MUTE\n"
  - "GET OUT-*.SRC\n"
  - "GET OUT-*.SRC_CHANNEL\n"
  - "GET OUT-*.OUTPUT_MODE\n"
  - "GET OUT-*.DELAY.TIME\n"
  - "GET OUT-*.DELAY.BYPASS\n"
  - "GET OUT-*.EQ.BYPASS\n"
  - "GET OUT-*.PRESET.NAME\n"
  - "GET OUT-*.PRESET.LOCKED\n"
  - "GET ROUT-*.SRC\n"
  - "GET ROUT-*.SRC_CHANNEL\n"
  - "GET ROUT-*.GAIN\n"
  - "GET IN-*.NAME\n"
  - "GET IN-*.GAIN\n"
  - "GET IN-*.SENS\n"
  - "GET IN-*.STEREO\n"
  - "GET IN-*.HPF_ENABLE\n"
  - "GET IN-*.EQ.BYPASS\n"
  - "GET MIX-*.NAME\n"
  - "GET MIX-*.GAIN-100\n"
  - "GET MIX-*.GAIN-101\n"
  - "GET MIX-*.GAIN-102\n"
  - "GET MIX-*.GAIN-103\n"
  - "GET MIX-*.GAIN-104\n"
  - "GET MIX-*.GAIN-105\n"
  - "GET MIX-*.GAIN-106\n"
  - "GET MIX-*.GAIN-107\n"
  - "GET MIX-*.GAIN-200\n"
  - "GET MIX-*.GAIN-201\n"
  - "GET MIX-*.GAIN-300\n"
  - "GET MIX-*.GAIN-301\n"
  - "GET MIX-*.GAIN-302\n"
  - "GET MIX-*.GAIN-303\n"
  - "GET MIX-*.GAIN-400\n"
  - "GET VC-*.NAME\n"
  - "GET VC-*.VALUE\n"
  - "GET SYSTEM.STATUS.STATE\n"
  - "GET SYSTEM.STATUS.SIGNAL_IN\n"
  - "GET SYSTEM.STATUS.SIGNAL_OUT\n"
  - "GET SYSTEM.STATUS.LAN\n"
  - "GET SYSTEM.STATUS.WIFI\n"
  - "GET API_VERSION\n"
  - "GET SYSTEM.DEVICE.VENDOR_NAME\n"
  - "GET SYSTEM.DEVICE.MODEL_NAME\n"
  - "GET SYSTEM.DEVICE.SERIAL\n"
  - "GET SYSTEM.DEVICE.FIRMWARE\n"
  - "GET SYSTEM.DEVICE.FIRMWARE_DATE\n"
  - "GET SYSTEM.DEVICE.MAC\n"
  - "GET SYSTEM.DEVICE.WIFI_MAC\n"
  - "GET SYSTEM.DEVICE.HWID\n"
  - "GET SYSTEM.DEVICE.SWID\n"
  - "GET SETUP.SYSTEM.DEVICE_NAME\n"
  - "GET SETUP.SYSTEM.VENUE_NAME\n"
  - "GET SETUP.SYSTEM.CUSTOMER_NAME\n"
  - "GET SETUP.SYSTEM.INSTALLER_NAME\n"
  - "GET SETUP.SYSTEM.CONTACT_INFO\n"
  - "GET SETUP.SYSTEM.INSTALL_DATE\n"
  - "GET SETUP.SYSTEM.ASSET_TAG\n"
  - "GET SETUP.SYSTEM.LOCATING\n"
  - "GET SETUP.POWER.POWER_ON\n"
  - "GET SETUP.POWER.MUTE_TIME\n"
  - "GET SETUP.POWER.STANDBY_TIME\n"
  - "GET GENERATOR.TYPE\n"
  - "GET GENERATOR.SINE.FREQ\n"
  - "GET GENERATOR.PINK.LPF_ENABLE\n"
  - "GET GENERATOR.PINK.LPF_FREQ\n"
  - "GET GENERATOR.PINK.HPF_ENABLE\n"
  - "GET GENERATOR.PINK.HPF_FREQ\n"
  - { send: "GET SYSTEM.DANTE.DEVICE_NAME\n", when: has_dante }
  - { send: "GET SYSTEM.DANTE.IP\n", when: has_dante }
  - { send: "GET SYSTEM.DANTE.MAC\n", when: has_dante }
  - { send: "GET SYSTEM.DANTE.FIRMWARE_VERSION\n", when: has_dante }
  - { send: "GET SYSTEM.DANTE.SOFTWARE_VERSION\n", when: has_dante }
  - { send: "GET SYSTEM.DANTE.LINK_SPEED\n", when: has_dante }
  - { send: "GET SYSTEM.DANTE.AES67_ENABLED\n", when: has_dante }
  - { send: "GET SYSTEM.DANTE.ENCODING\n", when: has_dante }
  - { send: "GET SYSTEM.DANTE.SAMPLE_RATE\n", when: has_dante }
  - { send: "GET SYSTEM.DANTE.CLOCK_STATE\n", when: has_dante }
  - { send: "GET SYSTEM.DANTE.MUTE_STATE\n", when: has_dante }

polling:
  # Everything else is pushed. The document does not say whether the status
  # registers are pushed on REG, and a wall controller's knob is an analog
  # reading, so these are read every Poll Interval as well.
  queries:
    - "GET SYSTEM.STATUS.STATE\n"
    - "GET SYSTEM.STATUS.SIGNAL_IN\n"
    - "GET SYSTEM.STATUS.SIGNAL_OUT\n"
    - "GET VC-*.VALUE\n"
    - { send: "GET SYSTEM.DANTE.CLOCK_STATE\n", when: has_dante }

liveness:
  # The document's own keep-alive (3.1.9): the TCP socket has no idle timeout,
  # so with a long Poll Interval nothing else would notice a unit that went
  # away without closing the connection. Every unit answers it in standby.
  send: "PING\n"
  expect: 'PONG'
  interval: 30
  timeout: 5
  max_failures: 2

simulator:
  # A change made in the Simulator UI is pushed to the driver, as the amplifier
  # pushes every register change to a REG subscriber.
  push_state: true
  # What the amplifier reports, under the driver's state keys, so the card is
  # right before a driver connects. Model and vendor are the document's own
  # examples (5.144, 5.147); a real unit's wording is not documented.
  initial_state:
    power: true
    system_state: "ON"
    signal_in: "SIGNAL"
    signal_out: "SIGNAL"
    model_name: "BLAZE-4"
    vendor_name: "Pascal"
    serial_number: "SN12345678"
    firmware_version: "2026.32.0"
    firmware_date: "2026-09-23"
    api_version: "1.5"
    hardware_id: 2
    software_id: 2
    mac_address: "40:11:DC:00:00:01"
    wifi_mac_address: "40:11:DC:00:00:02"
    lan_status: "192.168.64.100"
    wifi_status: ""
    device_name: "Amp-01"
    venue_name: "Acme Cafe"
    customer_name: "Acme"
    installer_name: "Acme AV"
    contact_info: "555-0100"
    install_date: "2026-11-03"
    asset_tag: "AMP-0001"
    locating: false
    power_on_mode: "NETWORK"
    mute_time: 300
    standby_time: 900
    generator_type: "PINK"
    sine_frequency: 1000.0
    pink_lpf_enable: false
    pink_lpf_frequency: 20000.0
    pink_hpf_enable: false
    pink_hpf_frequency: 20.0
    dante_device_name: "Amp-01-Dante"
    dante_ip: "192.168.64.101"
    dante_mac: "40:11:DC:00:00:03"
    dante_firmware_version: "4.2.1"
    dante_software_version: "4.2.1"
    dante_link_speed: 1000
    dante_aes67: false
    dante_encoding: "PCM24"
    dante_sample_rate: "48000"
    dante_clock_state: "LOCKED"
    dante_mute_state: ""
  # One dispatcher owns the whole grammar (GET with a wildcard, SET, INC,
  # SUBSCRIBE, PING, the power verbs): the per-command handlers the simulator
  # generates match exact strings, and the amplifier's answers depend on the
  # model (its zones, outputs and inputs come from the Zones, Outputs and
  # Dante Model settings) and on other registers (a zone with a wall volume
  # control refuses a level; a zone whose mute is not allowed refuses a mute).
  # Fidelity gaps, all undocumented behaviour: a SET is echoed to the client
  # that sent it whether or not it subscribed; meters (SUBSCRIBE DYN) are
  # acknowledged and never sent; a value outside a register's range is
  # refused E104 (the document does not say whether the amplifier clamps);
  # POWER_ON and POWER_OFF are accepted in every Power On Mode (the document
  # does not say which modes refuse them); REBOOT and FACTORY_DEFAULTS are
  # acknowledged and change nothing.
  command_handlers:
    - match: '(?s:.+)'
      handler: |
        _send = respond

        def _run():
            line = match.group(0).strip()
            if not line:
                return

            def truthy(v):
                return str(v).strip().lower() in ("1", "true", "yes", "on")

            zones = [z.strip().upper() for z in str(config.get("zones", "A,B,C,D")).split(",") if z.strip()]
            zones = [z for z in zones if z in ("A", "B", "C", "D", "E", "F", "G", "H")] or ["A", "B", "C", "D"]
            try:
                outs = int(str(config.get("output_count", 4)).strip())
            except ValueError:
                outs = 4
            if outs not in (1, 2, 4, 8):
                outs = 4
            dante = truthy(config.get("has_dante", False))
            inputs = [("100", "Analog 1"), ("101", "Analog 2"), ("102", "Analog 3"), ("103", "Analog 4"),
                      ("200", "S/PDIF 1"), ("201", "S/PDIF 1R")]
            if dante:
                inputs += [("300", "Dante 1"), ("301", "Dante 2"), ("302", "Dante 3"), ("303", "Dante 4")]
            inputs += [("400", "Noise Generator")]
            in_ids = [i for i, _ in inputs]
            mixes = ["1", "2"] if outs <= 2 else ["1", "2", "3", "4"]
            vcs = ["1", "2", "3", "4"]
            sources = ["0"] + in_ids + ["50" + str(int(m) - 1) for m in mixes]
            route_sources = (["0"] + [i for i in in_ids if i != "400"]
                             + ["50" + str(int(m) - 1) for m in mixes]
                             + ["100" + str(n) for n in range(min(len(zones), 4))])

            # register -> (kind, state key, default, writable, inc, lo, hi, choices)
            #   f float, b boolean, i integer, e enum, s string (quoted)
            REG = {}

            def reg(name, kind, key, default, w=True, inc=False, lo=None, hi=None, choices=None):
                REG[name] = (kind, key, default, w, inc, lo, hi, choices)

            for n, z in enumerate(zones):
                p = "zone." + z + "."
                reg("ZONE-" + z + ".NAME", "s", p + "name", "Zone " + z, hi=32)
                reg("ZONE-" + z + ".GAIN", "f", p + "gain", -20.0, inc=True, lo=-80.0, hi=0.0)
                reg("ZONE-" + z + ".GAIN_MIN", "f", p + "gain_min", -80.0, lo=-80.0, hi=0.0)
                reg("ZONE-" + z + ".GAIN_MAX", "f", p + "gain_max", 0.0, lo=-80.0, hi=0.0)
                reg("ZONE-" + z + ".MUTE", "b", p + "mute", False)
                reg("ZONE-" + z + ".MUTE_ENABLE", "b", p + "mute_enable", True)
                reg("ZONE-" + z + ".PRIMARY_SRC", "i", p + "source", int(in_ids[n % 4]), choices=sources)
                reg("ZONE-" + z + ".STEREO", "b", p + "stereo", False)
                reg("ZONE-" + z + ".GPIO_VC", "i", p + "gpio_vc", 0, choices=["0", "1", "2", "3", "4"])
                reg("ZONE-" + z + ".DUCK.MODE", "e", p + "duck_mode", "OFF", choices=["OFF", "DUCKER", "OVERRIDE"])
                reg("ZONE-" + z + ".PRIORITY-2.SRC", "i", p + "priority_2_source", 0, choices=sources)
                reg("ZONE-" + z + ".PRIORITY-3.SRC", "i", p + "priority_3_source", 0, choices=sources)
                reg("ZONE-" + z + ".COMPRESSOR.BYPASS", "b", p + "compressor_bypass", False)
            for n in range(1, outs + 1):
                o = str(n)
                p = "output." + o + "."
                reg("OUT-" + o + ".NAME", "s", p + "name", "Output " + o, hi=32)
                reg("OUT-" + o + ".GAIN", "f", p + "gain", 0.0, inc=True, lo=-30.0, hi=15.0)
                reg("OUT-" + o + ".MUTE", "b", p + "mute", False)
                reg("OUT-" + o + ".SRC", "z", p + "zone", zones[(n - 1) % len(zones)], choices=[""] + zones)
                reg("OUT-" + o + ".SRC_CHANNEL", "e", p + "channel", "S", choices=["L", "R", "S"])
                reg("OUT-" + o + ".OUTPUT_MODE", "e", p + "mode", "70V", choices=["OFF", "8R", "70V", "100V", "BTL"])
                reg("OUT-" + o + ".DELAY.TIME", "f4", p + "delay", 0.0, lo=0.0, hi=0.1)
                reg("OUT-" + o + ".DELAY.BYPASS", "b", p + "delay_bypass", True)
                reg("OUT-" + o + ".EQ.BYPASS", "b", p + "eq_bypass", False)
                reg("OUT-" + o + ".PRESET.NAME", "s", p + "preset_name", "Factory Preset", w=False, hi=64)
                reg("OUT-" + o + ".PRESET.LOCKED", "b", p + "preset_locked", False, w=False)
                reg("ROUT-" + o + ".SRC", "i", p + "route_source", 0, choices=route_sources)
                reg("ROUT-" + o + ".SRC_CHANNEL", "e", p + "route_channel", "S", choices=["L", "R", "S"])
                reg("ROUT-" + o + ".GAIN", "f", p + "route_gain", 0.0, lo=-40.0, hi=20.0)
            for i, label in inputs:
                p = "input." + i + "."
                gen = i == "400"
                reg("IN-" + i + ".NAME", "s", p + "name", label, hi=32)
                reg("IN-" + i + ".GAIN", "f", p + "gain", -20.0 if gen else 0.0, inc=True,
                    lo=-48.0 if gen else -15.0, hi=0.0 if gen else 15.0)
                if i.startswith("1"):
                    reg("IN-" + i + ".SENS", "e", p + "sensitivity", "4DBU", choices=["14DBU", "4DBU", "-10DBV", "MIC"])
                reg("IN-" + i + ".STEREO", "b", p + "stereo", False)
                reg("IN-" + i + ".HPF_ENABLE", "b", p + "hpf_enable", False)
                reg("IN-" + i + ".EQ.BYPASS", "b", p + "eq_bypass", False)
            for m in mixes:
                p = "mix." + m + "."
                reg("MIX-" + m + ".NAME", "s", p + "name", "Mix " + m, hi=32)
                for i in in_ids:
                    reg("MIX-" + m + ".GAIN-" + i, "f", p + "level_" + i, -144.0, inc=True, lo=-144.0, hi=0.0)
            for v in vcs:
                p = "volume_control." + v + "."
                reg("VC-" + v + ".NAME", "s", p + "name", "Wall VC " + v, w=False, hi=32)
                reg("VC-" + v + ".VALUE", "f", p + "value", 50.0, w=False)
            reg("SYSTEM.STATUS.STATE", "e", "system_state", "ON", w=False)
            reg("SYSTEM.STATUS.SIGNAL_IN", "e", "signal_in", "SIGNAL", w=False)
            reg("SYSTEM.STATUS.SIGNAL_OUT", "e", "signal_out", "SIGNAL", w=False)
            reg("SYSTEM.STATUS.LAN", "s", "lan_status", "192.168.64.100", w=False)
            reg("SYSTEM.STATUS.WIFI", "s", "wifi_status", "", w=False)
            reg("API_VERSION", "s", "api_version", "1.5", w=False)
            reg("SYSTEM.DEVICE.VENDOR_NAME", "s", "vendor_name", "Pascal", w=False)
            reg("SYSTEM.DEVICE.MODEL_NAME", "s", "model_name", "BLAZE-" + str(outs), w=False)
            reg("SYSTEM.DEVICE.SERIAL", "s", "serial_number", "SN12345678", w=False)
            reg("SYSTEM.DEVICE.FIRMWARE", "s", "firmware_version", "2026.32.0", w=False)
            reg("SYSTEM.DEVICE.FIRMWARE_DATE", "s", "firmware_date", "2026-09-23", w=False)
            reg("SYSTEM.DEVICE.MAC", "s", "mac_address", "40:11:DC:00:00:01", w=False)
            reg("SYSTEM.DEVICE.WIFI_MAC", "s", "wifi_mac_address", "40:11:DC:00:00:02", w=False)
            reg("SYSTEM.DEVICE.HWID", "i", "hardware_id", 2, w=False)
            reg("SYSTEM.DEVICE.SWID", "i", "software_id", 2, w=False)
            for name, key in (("DEVICE_NAME", "device_name"), ("VENUE_NAME", "venue_name"),
                              ("CUSTOMER_NAME", "customer_name"), ("INSTALLER_NAME", "installer_name"),
                              ("CONTACT_INFO", "contact_info"), ("INSTALL_DATE", "install_date"),
                              ("ASSET_TAG", "asset_tag")):
                reg("SETUP.SYSTEM." + name, "s", key, "", hi=32)
            reg("SETUP.SYSTEM.LOCATING", "b", "locating", False)
            reg("SETUP.POWER.POWER_ON", "e", "power_on_mode", "NETWORK",
                choices=["AUDIO", "AUDIO_ECO", "AUDIO_DSP", "TRIGGER", "TRIGGER_ECO", "NETWORK"])
            reg("SETUP.POWER.MUTE_TIME", "i", "mute_time", 300, lo=0, hi=3600)
            reg("SETUP.POWER.STANDBY_TIME", "i", "standby_time", 900, lo=0, hi=3600)
            reg("GENERATOR.TYPE", "e", "generator_type", "PINK", choices=["PINK", "SINE"])
            reg("GENERATOR.SINE.FREQ", "f1", "sine_frequency", 1000.0, lo=20.0, hi=20000.0)
            reg("GENERATOR.PINK.LPF_ENABLE", "b", "pink_lpf_enable", False)
            reg("GENERATOR.PINK.LPF_FREQ", "f1", "pink_lpf_frequency", 20000.0, lo=20.0, hi=20000.0)
            reg("GENERATOR.PINK.HPF_ENABLE", "b", "pink_hpf_enable", False)
            reg("GENERATOR.PINK.HPF_FREQ", "f1", "pink_hpf_frequency", 20.0, lo=20.0, hi=20000.0)
            reg("ZONE.COUNT", "i", "zone_count", len(zones), w=False)
            reg("OUT.COUNT", "i", "out_count", outs, w=False)
            reg("IN.COUNT", "i", "in_count", len(in_ids), w=False)
            reg("MIX.COUNT", "i", "mix_count", len(mixes), w=False)
            reg("VC.COUNT", "i", "vc_count", len(vcs), w=False)
            if dante:
                for name, kind, key, default in (
                        ("DEVICE_NAME", "s", "dante_device_name", "Amp-01-Dante"),
                        ("IP", "s", "dante_ip", "192.168.64.101"),
                        ("MAC", "s", "dante_mac", "40:11:DC:00:00:03"),
                        ("FIRMWARE_VERSION", "s", "dante_firmware_version", "4.2.1"),
                        ("SOFTWARE_VERSION", "s", "dante_software_version", "4.2.1"),
                        ("LINK_SPEED", "i", "dante_link_speed", 1000),
                        ("AES67_ENABLED", "b", "dante_aes67", False),
                        ("ENCODING", "e", "dante_encoding", "PCM24"),
                        ("SAMPLE_RATE", "e", "dante_sample_rate", "48000"),
                        ("CLOCK_STATE", "e", "dante_clock_state", "LOCKED"),
                        ("MUTE_STATE", "s", "dante_mute_state", "")):
                    reg("SYSTEM.DANTE." + name, kind, key, default, w=False)

            # Seed the model's registers once per model, so the Simulator UI
            # shows what the amplifier would answer.
            sig = ",".join(zones) + "/" + str(outs) + "/" + str(dante)
            if state.get("_seeded_for") != sig:
                # A child's register, a count and the model name take the
                # model's value; any other amplifier value keeps what
                # initial_state or the UI gave it.
                model_keys = ("zone_count", "out_count", "in_count", "mix_count", "vc_count", "model_name")
                for _r in REG.values():
                    _key, _d = _r[1], _r[2]
                    if (_key.startswith(("zone.", "output.", "input.", "mix.", "volume_control."))
                            or _key in model_keys or state.get(_key) is None):
                        state[_key] = _d
                state["_seeded_for"] = sig

            def current(name):
                kind, key, default = REG[name][0], REG[name][1], REG[name][2]
                v = state.get(key)
                return default if v is None else v

            def fmt(name, v):
                kind = REG[name][0]
                if kind == "b":
                    return str(int(bool(v)))
                if kind in ("s", "z"):
                    return '"' + str(v) + '"'
                if kind == "i":
                    return str(int(v))
                if kind == "f":
                    return "%.2f" % float(v)
                if kind == "f1":
                    return "%.1f" % float(v)
                if kind == "f4":
                    return "%.4f" % float(v)
                return str(v)

            def value_line(name):
                return "+" + name + " " + fmt(name, current(name))

            def err(msg):
                _send("#" + line + "|" + msg + "\n")

            DYN = ("DYN.SIGNAL", "DYN.CLIP")
            parts = line.split(" ", 2)
            verb = parts[0]

            if verb == "PING" and len(parts) == 1:
                _send("PONG\n*PING\n")
                return
            if verb in ("SUBSCRIBE", "UNSUBSCRIBE"):
                topic = parts[1] if len(parts) > 1 else ""
                if topic not in ("", "*", "REG", "DYN"):
                    err("E104: Invalid Parameter Value")
                    return
                _send("*" + line + "\n")
                return
            if verb in ("POWER_ON", "POWER_OFF") and len(parts) == 1:
                state["system_state"] = "ON" if verb == "POWER_ON" else "STANDBY"
                state["power"] = verb == "POWER_ON"
                _send("*" + line + "\n")
                return
            if verb in ("REBOOT", "FACTORY_DEFAULTS") and len(parts) == 1:
                _send("*" + line + "\n")
                return

            if verb == "GET" and len(parts) == 2:
                pattern = parts[1]
                if "*" in pattern:
                    rx = re.compile("^" + re.escape(pattern).replace("\\*", "[^.]+") + "$")
                    names = [n for n in REG if rx.match(n)]
                    _send("".join(value_line(n) + "\n" for n in names) + "*" + line + "\n")
                    return
                if pattern in REG:
                    _send(value_line(pattern) + "\n*" + line + "\n")
                    return
                if pattern.endswith(DYN):
                    err("E108: No getter for parameter")
                    return
                err("E107: Unknown Parameter")
                return

            if verb in ("SET", "INC"):
                if len(parts) < 3:
                    err("E105: Invalid number of arguments")
                    return
                name, raw = parts[1], parts[2].strip()
                if "*" in name or name not in REG:
                    err("E109: No setter for parameter" if name.endswith(DYN) else "E107: Unknown Parameter")
                    return
                kind, key, default, writable, can_inc, lo, hi, choices = REG[name]
                if not writable:
                    err("E109: No setter for parameter")
                    return
                zone_gain = name.startswith("ZONE-") and name.endswith(".GAIN")
                if zone_gain:
                    zp = name[:-len("GAIN")]
                    if int(current(zp + "GPIO_VC")) != 0:
                        err("E126: Volume is controlled by GPIO volume control.")
                        return
                    lo = float(current(zp + "GAIN_MIN"))
                    hi = float(current(zp + "GAIN_MAX"))
                if verb == "INC":
                    if not can_inc:
                        err("E124: No INC for parameter")
                        return
                    try:
                        delta = float(raw)
                    except ValueError:
                        err("E104: Invalid Parameter Value")
                        return
                    new = float(current(name)) + delta
                    new = max(lo, min(hi, new))
                    state[key] = new
                    _send(value_line(name) + "\n*" + line + "\n")
                    return
                if kind == "b":
                    if raw not in ("0", "1", "T", "F", "TRUE", "FALSE"):
                        err("E104: Invalid Parameter Value")
                        return
                    value = raw in ("1", "T", "TRUE")
                    if name.endswith(".MUTE") and name.startswith("ZONE-") and value:
                        if not current(name[:-len("MUTE")] + "MUTE_ENABLE"):
                            err("E128: Mute disabled.")
                            return
                elif kind in ("s", "z"):
                    if raw.startswith('"'):
                        if len(raw) < 2 or not raw.endswith('"') or '"' in raw[1:-1]:
                            _send("#" + line + "|Parse Error\n")
                            return
                        raw = raw[1:-1]
                    elif " " in raw:
                        err("E105: Invalid number of arguments")
                        return
                    if kind == "z":
                        if raw not in choices:
                            err("E104: Invalid Parameter Value")
                            return
                    elif name.endswith(".NAME") and not raw:
                        err("E131: String is empty")
                        return
                    elif hi is not None and len(raw) > hi:
                        err("E119: String is too long")
                        return
                    value = raw
                elif kind == "e":
                    if raw not in choices:
                        err("E104: Invalid Parameter Value")
                        return
                    value = raw
                elif kind == "i":
                    try:
                        value = int(raw)
                    except ValueError:
                        err("E104: Invalid Parameter Value")
                        return
                    if choices is not None and str(value) not in choices:
                        err("E104: Invalid Parameter Value")
                        return
                    if lo is not None and not (lo <= value <= hi):
                        err("E104: Invalid Parameter Value")
                        return
                else:
                    try:
                        value = float(raw)
                    except ValueError:
                        err("E104: Invalid Parameter Value")
                        return
                    if zone_gain:
                        value = max(lo, min(hi, value))
                    elif lo is not None and not (lo <= value <= hi):
                        err("E104: Invalid Parameter Value")
                        return
                state[key] = value
                # The echo every REG subscriber gets, then the caller's ack.
                _send(value_line(name) + "\n*" + line + "\n")
                return

            _send("#" + line + "|Command Not Recognized\n")

        _run()
